      "Canadian Broker-Dealers",
      "A Canadian broker-dealer with an office in a state must register there. Without an office, it can use a limited registration if its clients in the state are only:\n• Institutional investors.\n• Current customers who live in Canada and are in the state for 6 months or less.\n• Self-directed, tax-advantaged retirement plans held in Canada, where the customer is the holder or contributor.\n\nA limited registration is not a full state registration. Its agents serving only these clients can also use a limited registration. To get one, the broker-dealer must:\n• File an application and a consent to service of process, and pay a fee.\n• Show it is in good standing and registered where it is located.\n• Make records of its business in the state available to the Administrator.\n• Tell the Administrator about any criminal action against it.\n• Tell its clients in the state that it is not subject to all of the state's rules.",
